{"step_index":236,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-31T17:02:27Z","content":"The FastAPI app can now be started from the **project root** (the folder that contains `appresso_analysis`).  \n\n### How to run\n\n```powershell\n# From the project root (C:\\Users\\juan2\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\23eabdbc-225e-4c28-8288-af4260aef6b7)\n.\\appresso_analysis\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1      # activate the virtual environment\nuvicorn appresso_analysis.app:app --reload\n```\n\nIf the server starts without import errors, open a browser at <http://127.0.0.1:8000>. You should see the simple HTML form. Selecting a size and clicking **Ejecutar análisis** will:\n\n* generate synthetic orders,\n* persist them in SQLite,\n* run the algorithm counters,\n* compute the growth‑weeks model,\n* perform the NumPy regression prediction, and\n* write an `operation_counts.csv` file with the operation‑count summary.\n\nThe JSON response also contains a **download link** (`/download/operation_counts.csv`) so you can retrieve the CSV.\n\n### Things to verify\n\n| Check | Expected outcome |\n|------|-------------------|\n| Server starts (`uvicorn ...`) | No `ModuleNotFoundError` or syntax errors. |\n| `http://127.0.0.1:8000` loads the form | HTML page displayed. |\n| Submitting the form returns JSON | Contains keys `size`, `find_comparisons`, `total_additions`, `recursive_calls`, `recursive_additions`, `growth_weeks`, `prediction_2_5_days`, `prediction_7_days`, `csv_download`. |\n| Clicking the CSV link downloads a file | `operation_counts.csv` with a header line and one data row. |\n\nIf any of these steps fail, let me know the exact error message and we’ll fix it."}
